=== Point 2: reopened controls, both themes, real focus, ≥3:1 + coherence ===

Harness: worktree server on :8217 (`scripts/whatif-verify.sh start 8217`,
throwaway data/backup copies; live :8080 confirmed unreachable before AND
after this run — untouched). Playwright (chromium-1243, `--no-sandbox`,
1300×900) scripts in scratch `node/` (`lib.js`, `measure4.js`). Dark mode
via a real `#theme-toggle` click + `page.reload()`. Real-focus methodology
reused attempt 3's validated technique: one genuine `page.keyboard.press
('Tab')` first (establishes Chromium's real `:focus-visible` keyboard
modality for the page), then `el.focus()` on the exact named target — this
is the same technique attempt 3 (BK3.3 verdict) verified produces pixel-
identical rendering to a genuine Tab landing.

Targets: `#wf-tab-overview` and `#wf-tab-cashflow` (What-If tabs, one more
than required), `#insights-tab-trends` (`/insights?start=2026-06-01&end=
2026-06-30`), `#wf-collapse-money-toggle` (What-If collapse toggle) — all
four confirmed via computed style to carry BOTH `outline: solid
rgb(accent) 2px 2px` (theme-appropriate accent) AND `boxShadow: rgb(255,
255, 255) 0px 0px 0px 2px` in both themes (`measure4.json`).

Pixel methodology (`analyze4.py`, same relative-luminance WCAG contrast
formula as attempt 3): 16-20px-padded crop screenshot per target, scan
outward from each of 4 border edges (top/bottom/left/right), sampling
1px out (inner/white band) and 4px out (outer/accent band), background
found by scanning to a stability plateau (two consecutive equal samples).
Reports per-direction inner-vs-bg, outer-vs-bg, and the max; overall_max is
the max across all 4 directions.

  light  wf-tab-overview        overall_max = 5.76   (outer accent-vs-card
                                                        rgb(79,70,229) vs
                                                        rgb(245,245,244))
  light  wf-tab-cashflow         overall_max = 5.76
  light  insights-tab-trends     overall_max = 5.76
  light  wf-collapse-money-toggle overall_max = 6.29  (outer vs white card)
  dark   wf-tab-overview         overall_max = 17.49  (inner white-vs-card)
  dark   wf-tab-cashflow         overall_max = 17.49
  dark   insights-tab-trends     overall_max = 17.49
  dark   wf-collapse-money-toggle overall_max = 17.49

**Minimum 5.76:1, all 8 readings ≥3:1 — requirement (i) met in both
themes.** (One direction-specific artefact noted for the record: on
`right` for the two What-If tabs in light mode, and `bottom`/`right` for
`insights-tab-trends`, the inner/outer sample pair reads in the opposite
order from the other 3 directions — sub-pixel/anti-aliasing rounding at a
fractional box edge (e.g. `x: 447.5`), not a real gap; visually confirmed
below. It does not change the max, which is what the ≥3:1 requirement
turns on.)

Coherence (ii), visually confirmed via 6x-nearest-upscaled crops
(`*-6x.png` in the scratch dir):
- `dark-wf-tab-overview-6x.png`, `dark-insights-tab-trends-6x.png`: a
  crisp, continuous, concentric two-band ring — white band flush with the
  button, accent band immediately outside it, on all 4 sides, no gap, no
  double-line artefact.
- `dark-wf-collapse-money-toggle-6x.png`, `light-wf-collapse-money-toggle-
  6x.png`: same coherent ring on a 405px-wide element spanning most of the
  card width — NOT clipped by the card/panel ancestor, corners intact.
- `light-wf-tab-overview-6x.png`, `light-wf-tab-cashflow-6x.png`: the ring
  is a continuous unbroken rectangle around the button; the white inner
  band is visually indistinguishable from the near-white page/card
  background (expected — attempt 3 already characterized this as
  "imperceptible in light mode, white-on-white") but there is no gap
  artefact and no clipping.
- The visually thicker band at the BOTTOM of `wf-tab-overview` and
  `insights-tab-trends` in both themes is NOT part of the focus ring: both
  are their tablist's currently-ACTIVE tab, and `.wf-tab-active { border-
  bottom-color: rgb(79 70 229); }` / `.dark .wf-tab-active { border-
  bottom-color: rgb(129 140 248); }` (`web/static/css/styles.css:224-231`,
  pre-existing, predates BK3, unchanged) puts a 2px accent bottom border on
  the element's own border-box, which the ring is drawn from/around — this
  is the active-tab underline merging visually with the ring's bottom
  band, present on master too for the identical reason, not a BK3 defect.
  `#wf-tab-cashflow` (not the active tab) shows the ring with no such
  merge, confirming the bottom-band appearance is `.wf-tab-active`, not a
  ring-rendering defect.
- No ring was cut off by the tab strip's own `border-b` (the tablist
  wrapper's `border-b border-gray-200`): the wrapper has no `overflow`
  property and the tabs' outline (offset 2px, extending to 4px out) is
  fully visible past the wrapper's bottom border in every screenshot.

